. It should embed content properly, but to be cautious, I’ll add a fallback using the <picture> tag. The existing favicon indicates that assets from the public folder should be served. I think the <img> tag might be caching, so I’ll include explicit width and height. I'll create a new component, BrandLogo, which attempts to load the image and incorporates a fallback emoji or text if it fails. I’ll also add the onError method for extra safety. Finally, I’ll suggest the user refresh after these changes.**Addressing potential file path issues**

I think a missing file path might be the problem, so I want to check if index.html references /logo-isoedre.png — but it looks like it doesn’t. I’ll create a small component named BrandLogo in src/components/branding/BrandLogo.tsx that renders an image with an onError handler to switch the source to /favicon.ico or /placeholder.svg. I’ll apply a class for size and ensure the image exists in the public directory. I’ll also handle the AppHeader import and set up the necessary props while following guidelines for file creation. Finally, I'll prepare to implement the changes without heavy formatting and remind the user to refresh.</think>Je vois pourquoi ça peut ne pas s’afficher selon l’environnement. J’ajoute un petit composant BrandLogo avec un fallback automatique si le fichier /logo-isoedre.png n’est pas accessible, et je l’utilise dans le header.

<dyad-write path="src/components/branding/BrandLogo.tsx" description="Petit composant logo avec fallback si l’image ne charge pas">
import React from "react";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

type Props = {
  className?: string;
  size?: number; // px
  alt?: string;
};

const BrandLogo: React.FC<Props> = ({ className, size = 24, alt = "Logo ISOEDRE" }) => {
  const [src, setSrc] = React.useState<string>("/logo-isoedre.png");

  return (
    <img
      src={src}
      alt={alt}
      width={size}
      height={size}
      className={cn("rounded-md", className)}
      draggable={false}
      decoding="async"
      loading="eager"
      onError={() => setSrc("/placeholder.svg")}
    />
  );
};

export default BrandLogo;